---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { AUDIT_DATE, AUDIT_DATE_ISO, officialUrl, site, taglines } from '../content/site';
import { faq } from '../content/faq';
import { faqPage, softwareApplication, webPage } from '../lib/schema';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).href;
---

<Base
  title="ClientOS FAQ: Self-Hosted Client Portal Questions Answered"
  description="Every question agencies ask about ClientOS: what self-hosted means, what it costs, server requirements, white-label, migration, backups, and whether it is open source."
  og="og/faq.png"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: `${base}/` }, { label: 'FAQ' }]}
  schema={[
    webPage({
      url: canonical,
      name: 'ClientOS FAQ',
      description: 'Questions and answers about the self-hosted ClientOS client portal.',
      modified: AUDIT_DATE_ISO,
    }),
    faqPage(faq),
    softwareApplication(canonical),
  ]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h1>{faq.length} questions agencies ask</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every answer below is a restatement of something getclientos.com or its documentation
        states, and each one names where to check it. Where the site says nothing on a subject, the
        answer says that instead of filling the gap.
      </p>
      <p class="meta" style="margin-top:1.25rem">{taglines[0]}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
      <FaqList items={faq} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-raised">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What getclientos.com does not say</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A fair FAQ has to include the questions it cannot answer. These were all looked for on
        {AUDIT_DATE} and are not published anywhere on the official site — so this one does not
        answer them either. Ask the ClientOS team directly if any of them decide your purchase.
      </p>
      <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <li>
          <strong>What renewing updates costs.</strong> The site says ClientOS keeps running on your
          version and that you can renew for newer releases, but publishes no renewal price.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Whether there is a refund policy.</strong> No refund window or guarantee is
          stated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How many agencies run it.</strong> No customer count, revenue figure, rating or
          review score is published. One named case study is — Dot Mirror, a link building agency —
          and we treat it as the vendor’s own claim rather than independent proof.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Compliance and certification.</strong> No SOC 2, ISO 27001 or GDPR certification
          claim, and no data processing agreement, is published. Self-hosting changes who the data
          controller and processor are, which may be the point for you — but it is a question for
          your own counsel, not something the site answers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An uptime SLA.</strong> None is stated, and on a self-hosted product uptime is
          mostly your server’s, not the vendor’s.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A public API reference.</strong> The API runs on your own domain at
          <code>/v1</code> as part of the product, but no API documentation is published.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Whether there is a mobile app.</strong> None is mentioned. The docs describe the
          client portal working on a phone, in a browser.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="meta" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        The full list of gaps is in
        <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/UNVERIFIED.md`} rel="noopener">UNVERIFIED.md</a> in this
        repository, together with the competitor facts we could not check.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Still deciding?</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <a class="card card-link" href={`${base}/pricing/`}>
          <h3>What it really costs</h3>
          <p>
            The four licence prices, plus every other line of the actual bill — server, domain,
            email, gateway fees — including the ones ClientOS does not charge for.
          </p>
          <span class="card-more">Pricing summary →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card card-link" href={`${base}/install/`}>
          <h3>What self-hosting involves</h3>
          <p>
            The real work, in order: server, DNS, the command, browser setup, email, payments — and
            the backup schedule you have to add yourself.
          </p>
          <span class="card-more">Install guide →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card card-link" href={`${base}/alternatives/`}>
          <h3>How it compares</h3>
          <p>
            Against Wayfront, Zendo and Agency Handy, from each vendor’s own published pricing —
            including who should stay where they are.
          </p>
          <span class="card-more">Comparisons →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card card-link" href={officialUrl('faq_official')}>
          <h3>Ask them directly</h3>
          <p>
            The official site’s own FAQ and contact form. A person replies within one working day,
            with payment details or a demo if you ask for one.
          </p>
          <span class="card-more">getclientos.com →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta utm="faq" />
</Base>
